{"step_index":3600,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T19:29:31Z","thinking":"Examining the \"يحتاج مراجعة\" section, discrepancies are evident in requested versus available quantities. Line 4 shows a mismatch: 20 tablets of \"ديجستين\" are requested, but the available stock doesn't specify the count. Line 5 similarly highlights a quantity discrepancy with \"ايفاستين,\" with the request specifying \"2 strips\" but the available stock only noting \"tablets\". The differences in tablet counts are key.\n\n\nDiscrepancies extend to other rows in \"يحتاج مراجعة\", specifically rows 9, 16, and 19, where requested quantities (ampoules, films, strips) are specified, but the available stock lacks this detail. This suggests a pattern: the system flags entries where the exact quantity isn't explicitly stated in the available stock, even if the standard commercial packaging implicitly implies the quantity (like \"ديجستين\"). Row 21 shows it correctly identified a typo as well. This points to overly strict matching on quantity specification.\n\n\nThe system's strict quantity matching is causing false positives in the review section, flagging items that are actually matches based on standard packaging.  A revised matching rule, incorporating implied pack counts for known formulations, would significantly reduce the \"يحتاج مراجعة\" count. Further investigation into the total item counts is necessary, as there is a discrepancy between requested items and the total rows in the spreadsheet.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"d:\\miniconda3\\envs\\venv\\python.exe -c \"\nimport openpyxl\nfrom collections import Counter\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook(r'd:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\data\\processes\\PROC-001\\input_shortages\\0913.xlsx')\nws = wb['ورقة2']\ndrugs = [ws.cell(r, 2).value for r in range(7, ws.max_row+1) if ws.cell(r, 2).value]\nprint('Total rows:', len(drugs))\nprint('Unique drugs:', len(set(drug