{"step_index":3606,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T19:30:03Z","thinking":"The dataset contains 993 rows, but only 592 unique drug names, indicating significant duplication. It's crucial to understand why the summary used the values from cells B3, B4, and B5 for calculation of the total.\n\n\nCell B3 represents warehouse-specific matches, leading to double-counting of drugs present in multiple warehouses. The potential overlap between \"needs review\" and \"not found\" categories further complicates a simple sum. Directly adding B3, B4, and B5 does not accurately represent either the total raw shortages or unique drugs. To provide a clear summary, structuring it to distinguish between the original input rows (993) and unique drug counts (592) is crucial.\n\n\n`متطابق + يحتاج مراجعة + لم يعثر عليه = 592` confirms the unique drug count is accurately represented, and that there's no overlap in categories. The \"needs review\" items, totaling 140, arise from discrepancies such as differences in the number of tablets, strips, or ampoules between the requested and available items. Examining the \"تفاصيل المخازن\" reveals item counts supplied by each warehouse.\n\n\nThe \"needs review\" flag arises from overly strict adherence to pack size specification. Standard pack sizes in Egyptian pharmacies are being misclassified as discrepancies when the warehouse listing omits an item count but implicitly matches the standard. The system should distinguish between genuine differences in strength, dosage form, or active drug brand versus variations in pack size for the same product. Also, trade brands versus generics should be evaluated.\n\n\nAnalyzing specific examples, the \"needs review\" categorization appears overly sensitive to pack size. Standard pack counts should be considered automatic matches when explicitly requested pack sizes are not stated in the listing. Explicit number discrepancies should be the only trigger for a \"review\" status. This rule will significantly reduce the review list.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Inspect not found items","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import openpyxl\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfile_path = Path(r\"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\data\\processes\\PROC-001\\results_PROC-001.xlsx\")\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook(file_path, data_only=True)\nws = wb[\"لم يُعثر عليه\"]\n\nprint(f\"Total rows in 'لم يُعثر عليه': {ws.max_row}\")\nprint(\"\\n--- First 25 items in 'لم يُعثر عليه' ---\")\nfor r in range(2, 27):\n    print(f\"  {ws.cell(r, 1).value}\")\n","Description":"Inspect not found items in Excel","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\scratch\\inspect_not_found.py","toolAction":"Create inspect_not_found.py","toolSummary":"Check items in not found sheet"}}]}
