{"step_index":3618,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T19:30:59Z","thinking":"The search across all warehouse lists yielded zero matches for the provided medicine names. This indicates these specific items are definitively absent from the inventory represented in the six PDF lists provided. The lists, therefore, are unlikely to be related to those particular medicines.\n\n\nThe provided warehouse lists represent *specific cash discount or item-specific inventories*, not a comprehensive directory of all registered drugs in Egypt. The total unique items across all five warehouses are estimated at only 1,500 to 2,000, significantly smaller than the full national registry. The Excel file lists 993 customer orders, but these order multiple quantities of only 592 unique drug names; a high level of item duplication explains the row count difference.\n\n\nThe Excel formula erroneously sums individual matched rows across warehouses, leading to an inflated total of 646 due to duplicate counting of items present in multiple warehouses. The correct summary must use unique item counts and avoid double-counting; the correct calculation should sum unique items in each category: matched, needing review, and not found. The suggested Excel fix uses this approach, summing unique item counts to match the input row numbers.\n\n\nThe model flagged items for review because the warehouse lists omitted explicit quantities (e.g., \"20 قرص\"). This resulted in many items being classified as needing manual inspection when the standard packaging is known. The model's approach appears overly strict. Adjusting this rule in the system should reduce the review queue.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py","EndLine":45,"StartLine":20,"toolAction":"View Rule 3 in coordinator prompt","toolSummary":"Check packaging rule in prompt"}}]}
{"step_index":3619,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T19:31:11Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T22:31:11+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T22:31:12+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/src/fast_match/coordinator.py`\nTotal Lines: 333\nTotal Bytes: 17330\nShowing lines 20 to 45\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n20:    - Note equivalencies: 1000mg = 1gm (1000مجم = 1جم), 500mg = 0.5gm, 0.25mg = ربع (250mcg).\n21: \n22: 2. DOSAGE FORM:\n23:    - If the requested drug specifies a dosage form (tablets vs syrup vs cream vs drops vs ampoules/injections) and the candidate is a DIFFERENT form (e.g. ampoule vs capsule, or syrup vs tablet):\n24:      YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n25: \n26: 3. PACKAGING, PACK SIZE, TABLET COUNT & WHOLESALE UNITS (MATCH vs REVIEW):\n27:    - \"match\": Exact same active drug brand, same strength, same dosage form.\n28:      If pack size/count is identical (e.g. \"فولتارين ٣ امبولات\" matching \"فولتارين ٣ امبولات/نوفارتس\", \"كونتافين ١ شريط\" matching \"كونتافين ١ شريط/اكاديميا\") OR not specified in the requested shortage (e.g. \"سيتال اقراص\" matching \"سيتال اقراص 20 قرص\", or \"كليكسان 40 حقن\" matching \"كليكسان 40مجم-84\"), return \"status\": \"match\".\n29:      CRITICAL: If the numbers/counts are identical (even if written in Arabic numerals ٣ vs 3) or the only difference is the manufacturer name (/نوفارتس, /اكاديميا, /ايبيكو), THIS IS A 100% MATCH. NEVER mark as review!\n30:    - \"review\": Same active drug brand, same strength, same dosage form, BUT different pack size, tablet count, or packaging variant (e.g. requested 15 tablets vs candidate 60 tablets, requested 24 tablets vs candidate 48 tablets, requested medium vs candidate large / باكو 25).\n31:      In this case, return \"status\": \"review\" AND provide a clear Arabic explanation in \"reason\" (e.g. \"اختلاف عدد الأقراص: المطلوب 15 قرص والمرشح 60 قرص\" or \"اختلاف الحجم: المطلوب وسط والمرشح كبير باكو 25\").\n32: \n33: 4. TRADE BRAND vs GENERIC / ALTERNATIVE (بديل أو مثيل):\n34:    - \"match\": Both items must have the SAME commercial trade brand name (e.g. Panadol matching Panadol, Zovirax matching Zovirax).\n35:    - \"review\": If the candidate has the SAME active ingredient and SAME strength, but is a generic name or a DIFFERENT trade brand (e.g. requested trade brand \"رو اكيتان 20\" vs candidate generic \"ايزوتريتينوين 20\", or requested \"زوفيراكس 400\" vs candidate \"لوفير 400\"):\n36:      DO NOT mark as \"match\"! Return \"status\": \"review\" AND explain in \"reason\":\n37:      \"بديل تجاري / مثيل: نفس المادة الفعالة والتركيز ولكن الاسم التجاري مختلف (المطلوب: [اسم]، المتوفر: [اسم])\".\n38: \n39: 5. WHOLESALE & PACKAGING METADATA:\n40:    - Terms like \"باكو 25\" (pack of 25), \"كرتونه 100\" (carton of 100), \"سعر جديد\", \"سعر قديم\", \"س ج\", \"-84\", \"-50\", \"32ب\", \"/المهن\", \"/العامرية\" indicate wholesale packaging, distributor codes, or prices.\n41:    - Take them into account to distinguish listings, but if candidate matches the drug, form, and strength, accept it or mark review if wholesale pack quantity differs from requested.\n42: \n43: SCHEMA:\n44: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\n45: {\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
